#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hermes-mon — live terminal monitor for a Hermes Agent kanban board.

Shows, in a single terminal and without touching the gateway:

  · how many cards there are and in which state (planned, ready, running…),
  · which profile owns each one,
  · the log of every worker running RIGHT NOW, auto-tailed,
  · which Hermes instances are alive on the machine (gateway, dashboard,
    workers, chat sessions), with their PID and profile,
  · and whether anyone is actually dispatching — the failure mode that
    silently stalls a board for hours.

Panes follow the work: when a card finishes its pane disappears, when another
one starts its pane shows up. Several cards running at once share the screen.

Everything is read-only: the board database is opened with `mode=ro` and the
worker logs are followed by offset, like `tail -f`. Nothing is ever written.

Usage:
    hermes-mon                 # monitor the active board
    hermes-mon --pick          # choose the board first
    hermes-mon --profile foo   # only cards owned by profile `foo`
    hermes-mon --snapshot      # print one frame as plain text and exit

Requires Python 3.10+ and a Linux /proc. No third-party dependencies.
"""

